# API & Core Backend Principles

- Validate all incoming external data using `zod` schemas. Fail fast and return clean, structured error responses on validation failure.
- When receiving requests for heavy operations, validate the payload, enqueue the task via BullMQ, and immediately return a `202 Accepted` status with the job identifier.
- Environment variables (OpenRouter, Runway, AWS, Stripe, Redis) must be strictly validated at runtime startup using Zod. Never log or leak these keys.